# Flutter/Dart Conventions

## Naming

- Files: `snake_case.dart`; classes: `PascalCase`; private: `_camelCase`
- Services: `*Service`; utils: `*Utils`, `*Calculator`, `*Finder`, `*Gate`
- Storage keys: `snake_case` strings in `ContactStorageService`

## Imports

```dart
import '../models.dart';           // internal — relative
import 'package:provider/provider.dart';  // external — package
```

## Async + BuildContext

Guard every `context` use after `await`:

```dart
// ❌ BAD — context after async gap without guard
await someAsyncWork();
Navigator.of(context).pop();

// ✅ GOOD
await someAsyncWork();
if (!mounted) return;
Navigator.of(context).pop();

// ✅ GOOD — helper receiving BuildContext
if (upgrade == true && context.mounted) {
  await showUpgradeSheet(context);
}
```

`while (mounted)` alone is **not** enough before `showDialog` — add `if (!mounted) return;` immediately before each post-await context use.

## State management

- Screen state: fields on `State` + `setState`
- Pro/IAP only: `context.read<ProSubscriptionService>()` or `Consumer`
- Do **not** introduce new global state libraries without explicit request

## Services

Instantiate directly — no DI container:

```dart
final _storageService = ContactStorageService();
```

## API style

- `Color.withValues(alpha: 0.5)` not `withOpacity`
- Doc comments (`///`) on public utils and service methods
- Extract helpers to `lib/utils/` rather than growing `contacts_page.dart`
